<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Trump calls renewed Ukraine attacks on Russian oil refineries 'a disgrace'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79eb073a6279c673b4238c33dedd9a66ce7e793e49c5ca16703fb16b2b2b9c7a</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T01:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace--6cfecd7f8863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump called Ukraine's renewed strikes on Russian oil refineries a "disgrace" after Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky rejected his calls for an "energy ceasefire." Zelensky sought support from European allies earlier that day in Brussels on the sidelines of an EU summit. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Four dead, including three children, in Oregon school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a02ba6ede6f32c2a3dfffdb493c21313009625c9f70180df3f811f0e11dbf65</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:57:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead--5a6aa5ab65a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead" /></entry><entry><title>19 injured as minibus crashes into train at Channel Tunnel entrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74a945b5df9ca47a945da80b8676c8dad115e8586a3d3e65040d6ab36020c571</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance--79f37e5f8958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance" /><summary type="html">Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a624180c937a26570813e2d62a7d718028c6e1ab7e3bcc1eb74eca9158f1811</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal--9bcf5af8133a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal" /><summary type="html">France and Germany have backed looser EU emissions rules for carmakers and agreed to include Britain in a “made in Europe” scheme, in a provisional deal reached Thursday that could reshape the bloc’s automotive and climate policies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04e0f0f1c1578b1e8297166582405525839e87f80172d1390662fdf23c41101b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes--820569914737.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands, as tensions with Washington escalated over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Teen shooter kills three children and teacher at Oregon elementary school</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80c5fc35f4465084debb3608785bc058d59ff505e893cf44248f64294dccee2d</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead--5a6aa5ab65a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-two-hospitalised-after-shooting-at-oregon-elementary-school-gunman-dead" /><summary type="html">A 16-year-old gunman killed three children aged 5, 8 and 11, and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday before being killed by a community member who pursued him inside, police said. Two other people were wounded in the shooting.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Sally Rooney books cannot be sold in UK amid Palestine Action ban: publisher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:255ce5844615e43673e7660274efed89b571b0cb51fea9eb22381d16529a3ea5</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:15:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher--6528f0929ba4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher" /><summary type="html">Irish author Sally Rooney can no longer sell her books in the UK because of her support for the activist group Palestine Action, her publisher Faber said Wednesday. Rooney has previously expressed her support for the group, which was banned as a "terrorist" organisation by the UK government in July 2025. It is not banned in Ireland, where Rooney lives. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alan Greene, Professor of Constitutional Law and Human Rights at the Birmingham Law School.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Sally Rooney books cannot be sold in UK amid Palestine Action ban: publisher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:240428515a912a28a4a3ded1487e6c6fac37aa3e19de7e9d2a6c0369c377f375</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher--8cf5b8c94062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher" /><summary type="html">Irish author Sally Rooney can no longer sell her books in the UK because of her support for the activist group Palestine Action, her publisher Faber said Wednesday. Rooney has previously expressed her support for the group, which was banned as a "terrorist" organisation by the UK government in July 2025. It is not banned in Ireland, where Rooney lives. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alan Greene, Professor of Constitutional Law and Human Rights at the Birmingham Law School.</summary></entry><entry><title>Oxfam takes France to court over 'tax inequality': 'Problem' with tax system, public service funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a99ae385142bb87bdaeddd1bb021e3a3c2e2bd742f4cdd31404340c5315d0f</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:41:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261015-oxfam-takes-france-to-court-over-tax-inequality-problem-with-tax-system-public-service-fund--930b0f513f70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261015-oxfam-takes-france-to-court-over-tax-inequality-problem-with-tax-system-public-service-funding" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Layla Abdelké Yakoub, Tax Justice and Inequality Advocacy Officer at Oxfam France. "Today in France a billionaire pays less taxes proportionally than a nurse or a firefighter," explains Yakoub. She challenges the foundations of France's fiscal system, arguing that the growing concentration of wealth and preferential tax treatment of the ultra-rich are undermining the constitutional principle of equality before taxation. As Oxfam pursues legal action against the French state, Yakoub describes a widening disconnect between the government's efforts to attract investment and its ability to finance public services, address poverty and carve out an ecological transition.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>EU member states set for budget clash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4171991502b0fa89e65de6dd778ee9be8b66008bddc7f22f6b28c666fb53d5bb</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:33:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-member-states-set-for-budget-clash--22009c744091.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-member-states-set-for-budget-clash" /><summary type="html">European lawmakers have kicked off what's likely to be a long and fierce negotiation over the bloc's seven-year budget. Member states are divided on spending priorities, and pending elections in countries including France and Italy are adding pressure to the talks in Brussels. Also in the show - AI stocks lose a trillion dollars in this week's tech stock sell-off, and Ledger's CTO Charles Guillemet explains why AI is changing the security landscape.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia postpones major sporting events amid Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228347deaaa65ea7003bc7e19a16223dafbbbee213d274835b579c462efc4d42</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:31:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-postpones-major-sporting-events-amid-houthi-attacks--b77da744bba3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-postpones-major-sporting-events-amid-houthi-attacks" /><summary type="html">Several major sporting events in Saudi Arabia have been cancelled or postponed as a result of repeated deadly attacks from Iran-backed Houthi rebels against the Kingdom's airports and infrastructure. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Guy Barton, Visiting Fellow at Lancaster University and co-creator and co-host of The FootPol Podcast.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kinshasa braces for potential conflict as Kabila joins M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f3bc50d66fbbc0c278a2c251be710b488ab0f712b0005b84dab6d3a263bc4b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:29:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kinshasa-braces-for-potential-conflict-as-kabila-joins-m23--7a7b7a23cc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kinshasa-braces-for-potential-conflict-as-kabila-joins-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, as Joseph Kabila returns to centre stage with a new alliance with the M23 rebels, political leaders in Congo are having to choose sides. Also, the US is calling for restraint in Ethiopia as a rights group warns that the conflict in Tigray is already taking a toll on civilians. And the season of art fairs returns, we take a look at the rising international visibility of African contemporary art.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4113c0d6d770f2fa4715869aff187a9e9de075f3005adb79f8806f6d2af6ae05</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:03:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep--8a7157699d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep" /><summary type="html">Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthi attack on palace used by Yemen government in Aden kills five</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0edc782e3e5d8e19d18f38a1010b5b8645e261d19aaf8906147c3fbaee3c0f1e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:57:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthi-attack-on-palace-used-by-yemen-government-in-aden-kills-five--c8f66163cd30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261015-houthi-attack-on-palace-used-by-yemen-government-in-aden-kills-five" /><summary type="html">At least five people were killed and 16 wounded Thursday in a Houthi missile and drone attack on the palace located in Yemen's interim capital – the southern port city of Aden, used by the country's internationally recognised government, an official said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:432759f1861aaf5156e05dac8c16ed335bde7ad980ce95137496147492ba2829</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says--5033be605410.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".</summary></entry><entry><title>Fake AI images of protester go viral after woman punched at Trump's Ohio rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14ec61a5e9cca8032aca227943f2c3e7a236512064d246f7fadaacfd3e6a81a4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:47:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally--84322c184e38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fake-ai-images-of-protester-go-viral-after-woman-punched-at-trump-s-ohio-rally" /><summary type="html">A protester who heckled Donald Trump at his midterm rally in Youngstown, Ohio, was physically assaulted and removed from the event, but fake AI-generated photos recreating the incident are going viral online. The images carry digital watermarks identifying them as AI-generated. While footage confirms the woman was punched, there is no evidence to support Trump’s claim that the protester was "paid" to disrupt his speech, as he mocked the protester's weight. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8026b8d3ab64e2707d185d32eb871a6d80e8ee2f326e477c4aef6df11b2418c4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:04:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--33513f001314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Albania's leader defies calls to resign as student protesters rampage in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30d4f59199e138587bef2ef5f2f834a92253f9ca0066d5ca959f2157e37b2146</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:02:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital--247a1ee2a654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital" /><summary type="html">​Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Thursday rejected calls to resign as thousands of student-led protesters smashed windows and fought running battles with riot police firing water cannon and tear gas in the capital. The demonstrators accuse officials of corruption and neglecting education and say they are angry about the sale of parts of Albania's southern coastline to a luxury resort development backed ​by US President ‌Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Trump really pull the plug? Starlink restored but Ukraine's fate still uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1eea4af24a1743753f7e092e19968c9667528971d763d69c1370a001a71c9b0</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:38:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain--2088cc5dba32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain" /><summary type="html">Can a flick of a switch really be enough for Donald Trump and Elon Musk to end Ukraine's hopes of holding out against Russia? With Kyiv already reeling from daily strikes by Russia's new motor-powered drones, the United States decision to slow SpaceX Starlink service felt immediately Wednesday when air raid warnings failed.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro and wife Cilia Flores deny US torture charges as 'false accusations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81282ae0dd1883d47754e8be5502030f129b6491438f69e1fd9cafd95f0270d5</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:11:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusatio--a2d0e0fa417a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-and-wife-cilia-flores-deny-us-torture-charges-as-false-accusations" /><summary type="html">Ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores pleaded not guilty on Thursday to new torture charges brought against them by US authorities, calling them “false allegations". The couple has been held in a New York jail since their capture in early January and is facing a new indictment accusing them of conspiring to torture political opponents and US citizens.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f87e16a2d8c7d25ee57479241af8499bc618a32cd83ce5ce5e8b15078a5a9b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms--b38db7502a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Election delay 'a terrible disappointment', Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:809aeb325253672d047e2d18ac543c9eb60c13132f184dc53e3873ca9b679579</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:17:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says--df16dcb36eae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261015-election-delay-a-terrible-disappointment-palestinian-activist-samer-sinijlawi-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Palestinian activist Samer Sinijlawi called the postponement of the first legislative elections in 20 years to September 2027 "a terrible disappointment" for a generation that has never had a chance to vote. He also dismissed the citing of Israeli restrictions as an excuse, pointing instead to a "rejection" of change among ageing Palestinian leaders.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a5fe3623537efcb9bda9080beea2069e07289aca7e1cfb2a08f30be5393718</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:14:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-tal--b4d9641c071b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.</summary></entry><entry><title>India’s Cockroach movement: Protesters bypass internet blackout with Bluetooth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a566aaa94dd56bce13f0e952c1324107034741bcdd11514e0da2e2857a57719e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T15:29:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-india-s-cockroach-movement-protesters-bypass-internet-blackout-with-bluetooth--dfbcc10c75b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-india-s-cockroach-movement-protesters-bypass-internet-blackout-with-bluetooth" /><summary type="html">🇮🇳 On October 10, New Delhi faced a near-lockdown situation following a call for protests by Gen Z-led Cockroach Janta Party. Authorities imposed a 24-hour internet blackout, but protesters found ways around it.</summary></entry></feed>
